        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4de9776f-8bc1-5446-9a6a-28db44c46701",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bill Walton, John Wooden, Brad Nessler, Tom Tolbert\n- Organizations: UCLA Bruins, UCLA, ABC, NCAA\n- Events: 2003 NBA Finals\n- Awards: College Player of the Year Awards, NCAA national championships, Division I national titles\n\nFacts:\n- In the early 1970s, Bill Walton became known for playing for John Wooden's UCLA Bruins powerhouse team.\n- In the early 1970s, Bill Walton won three consecutive College Player of the Year Awards.\n- In the early 1970s, Bill Walton led the UCLA Bruins to two Division I national titles.\n- During a 12-year period as UCLA head coach, John Wooden won ten NCAA national championships, including a record seven straight titles.\n- John Wooden was nicknamed the \"Wizard of Westwood.\"\n- The 2003 NBA Finals were broadcast on U.S. television by ABC.\n- Brad Nessler, Bill Walton, and Tom Tolbert served as announcers for the 2003 NBA Finals broadcast.",
